course: dictionary
lesson: 3757
title: One word, many flutters
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: Flutter has more than one meaning, so the sentence around it tells you which one to use. «A flat sheet of paper flutters down slowly, but the same sheet screwed into a ball drops fast.» Here flutters means moves gently through the air, not flaps like a bird, because the paper is floating.
explain: «The cards were dead leaves fluttering down from the trees onto her face.» Leaves cannot flap their wings, so fluttering means moving lightly and gently back and forth as they fall. Ask yourself: what is moving, and how?
explain: Flutter can also describe a heart. If a character's heart flutters before a race, it beats fast and unevenly because of nerves or excitement. In everyday UK talk, a «flutter» is also a small, fun bet on a horse race. Betting is for adults only, so you will recognise it in books and news, not try it yourself.
fact: Flutter can mean to move wings quickly and lightly, as butterflies and moths do.
fact: Flutter can mean to move gently back and forth in the air, like a flag or leaves.
fact: Flutter can mean a heart beating fast and unevenly because of excitement or nerves.
fact: As a noun, «a flutter» is a small bet just for fun, and «in a flutter» means in a state of excitement.
fact: To check your meaning, put it into the sentence: «The leaves fluttered down» still makes sense with gently moving, but not with a small bet.
exercise: «A flat sheet of paper flutters down slowly, but the same sheet screwed into a ball drops fast.» What does flutters mean here? | *Moves gently and slowly through the air | Lands with a loud bang | Makes a small bet | Beats quickly, like a frightened heart
exercise: «The cards were dead leaves fluttering down from the trees onto her face.» Which movement does fluttering describe? | Shining brightly in the sun | Shouting loudly at the trees | *Light, gentle movement as the leaves fall | Fast, hard stamping on the ground
exercise: Jayden says, «My heart flutters before every test.» What does flutters mean? | *Beats fast and unevenly because he is nervous | Stops beating for a long time | Beats slowly and calmly, like when asleep | Flaps like a bird's wings
test: Lily is in a flutter before the school play. What does in a flutter mean? | *A state of excitement or nerves | A small bet on a horse race | Quiet and still, without any feeling | A hole in the ground
test: «The butterfly fluttered from flower to flower.» Which meaning of flutter fits here? | To fall heavily to the ground | *To move wings quickly and lightly | To beat fast because of nerves | To make a small bet
exam: Which sentence uses flutter to mean a small bet? | The leaves fluttered in the wind | *Dad likes to have a flutter on the horses | My heart fluttered on the stage | The butterfly fluttered its wings
